1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:05,800
"The AI fixed my robot."

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:11,300
But who grades it? The model that proposes
the fix is the same model that grades it.

3
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:16,000
That's grading your own homework —
and in robotics the stakes are heavier.

4
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:22,000
RoboWitness separates the roles:
the AI proposes.

5
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:28,000
The simulator runs deterministically at 60 Hz.
The policy never sees its true pose —
only delayed, noisy sensor data.

6
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:34,000
The oracle decides: it checks true geometry
and never reads the model's rationale.

7
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:40,000
Five good-looking candidates
took exams on frozen holdout sets.

8
00:00:40,500 --> 00:00:46,000
Five rejections — each sealed
in SHA-256 evidence.

9
00:00:46,500 --> 00:00:50,000
We never lowered the bar.

10
00:00:51,500 --> 00:00:56,000
The bar is the product.

11
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:10,000
Then we registered the next candidate
before its exam existed: MPC-lite.
The set was generated after registration.
On a single shot: 20 out of 20.

12
00:01:10,500 --> 00:01:20,000
Five gates clean — VERIFIED_IN_SIMULATION.
And an over-cautious control candidate
in the same run was still rejected.

13
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:30,000
RoboWitness.
If a result can't survive an independent
re-check, it isn't a result.
